# Prettier's default --ignore-path is BOTH .gitignore and .prettierignore (`prettier --help
# ignore-path`), so an entry is only needed here for paths git actually tracks. That is why
# `.claude/` and `.worc/` need a line below while `.worc-io/` does not — it is already gitignored.
# The corollary is the one to remember: anything in .gitignore is silently outside the format gate,
# which is why `tasks/` is not gated (P12.06 records why that is deliberate).
dist
coverage
.vitest
packages/**/dist

# Raw JSON.stringify(schema, null, 2) output (packages/core/src/engine/schema.ts); a byte-sync
# test (schema-generation.test.ts, R6) requires this file to match that output exactly, which
# collapses short arrays differently than Prettier's JSON formatting would.
packages/cli/schema.json

# Agent/orchestrator tooling config, not product surface — out of scope for this repo's format gate.
.worc/
.claude/
